A||||6||GT Bastard||Question on dying leather seats....||||4||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||12-01-2000||01:50 AM||||I'm picking up a set of 4th gen leather seats from a Formula Firebird tomorrow.  Question is this:  My interior is tan, but the seats are charcoal... I'm getting the seats cheap, and they're tough to find(and it's cheaper than fixing my fiero seats) so I want to keep them.  I've heard that it's not a big deal to have a vinyl shop dye them the correct color.  Anyone had any experience with this?  Sounds easier than changing the color of my interior.||||reg||4
Z||000001||fropuff||12-01-2000||06:00 PM||||I bought some vinyl dye from JC Whitney to do some door panels.  I also did a vinyl headliner that JC Whitney shipped to me incorrectly.  It turned out pretty nice.  I didn't get too well in the seams, so they can still be seen.  If you have a shop do it, you should be okay.  I don't know about the gray to tan, but someone else will know for sure.  I am thiking of getting some Firebird seats for my 86 GT later.  Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||12-01-2000||06:06 PM||||go to an automotive paint store. they have a special paint/dye that is made for vinyl and leather. make sure you clean and dry it very well first, also on seats make sure to use the clear protective coat of the same stuff. I like MarHyde brand if you can find it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||12-01-2000||07:47 PM||||GTB,<P>I have worked at several car dealerships either as a detailer or a salesman... I can guarantee that EVERY used car with leather seats has seen a spray can of leather "dye".  All it is is matte paint.  If I were you I would find a detailer and ask him (not his boss) if he would mind spraying your seats.  Offer him $20 + dye.  I guarantee it will be the easiest $20 he has ever made.  Seriously it will take them about 15 minutes to do a good job.  That way you don't have to worry about potentially screwing them up.  When they are done you can ship them to:  <P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>3301 Gol... oh never mind.  I know you just won't give them to me.  I have been a very good boy this year :~)<P>WTT3||||reg||14
Z||000004||terryk||12-01-2000||08:52 PM||||But only after they have gone through a complete and rigorous QA testing program at....<P>||||reg||10
